<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leo Gabalas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. <a href="/years/1204">1204</a>–<a href="/years/1240">1240</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Leo <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qabala">Gabalas</a> was a Byzantine Greek <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnates">magnate</a> who seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhodes">Rhodes</a> and nearby islands after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade">Fourth Crusade</a> broke up the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a> in 1204. He ruled them as an independent lord with the title of Caesar, recognising the Empire of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicaea">Nicaea</a> only loosely and making a treaty with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> in 1234. After his death around 1240 his brother John held Rhodes until Nicaea took direct control.</p></div>
